---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";

const lastUpdated = "August 18, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Account Deletion"
  description="How to request deletion of a Covey account and related data."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-[var(--section-y)]">
    <div class="eyebrow mb-3">Deletion</div>
    <h1 class="display t-h1 mb-4">Delete your Covey account</h1>
    <p class="font-mono text-ink-muted text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] mb-12">
      Last updated {lastUpdated}
    </p>

    <div class="card p-6 mb-12">
      <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
        You can request account deletion from the Covey app when signed in. If
        you cannot access your account, contact support from the email address
        tied to the account.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed text-lg">
      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">In the app</h2>
        <p>
          Open Covey, go to your profile or account settings, and choose the
          account deletion option. The app will ask you to confirm before the
          request is submitted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">By email</h2>
        <p>
          If you need help, email
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.emails.support}`} class="text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1">
            {SITE.emails.support}
          </a>
          with "Account deletion" in the subject. Please write from the email
          address on your Covey account so we can verify the request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">What deletion covers</h2>
        <p>
          Deletion is meant to remove or de-identify account information and
          personal content tied to your profile, including account details,
          profile information, and app data where removal is technically and
          legally possible.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="title-mono text-2xl text-ink mb-3">What may remain</h2>
        <p>
          Some records are kept for security, fraud prevention, legal
          obligations, backups, dispute handling, or safety investigations —
          including reports and enforcement records, so that a banned account
          cannot simply return. The
          <a href="/privacy#retention" class="text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1">retention table in our Privacy Policy</a>
          lists each category and why we keep it. Content that other people
          already received, such as messages or plan context, may not disappear
          from their accounts immediately.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
